From 69c81341b9d6079f3ab54dd8734807b9c57cb707 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TEX8 Monero Patch Integrator <monero-patches@tex8.local>
Date: Fri, 06 Nov 2026 16:50:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] wallet: repair stalled gRPC stripes without resetting healthy lanes

A stalled historical stripe blocks ordered delivery while the other lanes
hold already-downloaded blocks. Repair the exact remaining stripe on one
replacement stream, and resume that lane at its next original boundary.
Keep the original chunk deadline, a repair cooldown and the existing
near-tip, locator and fallback rules.

Start synchronous gRPC readers on their cancellable receive threads. Do
not tear down healthy lanes based on an adaptive sample from a repair.

